    citation: "Cal. Penal Code § 1320.5 (felony); § 1320 (misdemeanor)",
    keyRule: "California splits failure to appear by the underlying case: § 1320.5 applies when a person charged with or convicted of a felony and released on bail willfully fails to appear to evade the court's process, a felony punishable up to 3 years and a $10,000 fine. A separate statute, § 1320, covers the misdemeanor-case/own-recognizance-release version. A willful failure to appear within 14 days of the scheduled date creates a presumption that the absence was intended to evade the court.",
    penaltyClass: "Felony, up to 3 years and $10,000 fine (felony case); misdemeanor (misdemeanor case or OR release)",
