    keyRule: "A clean, four-tier felony ladder based purely on outcome and target rather than on intent variations: causing great bodily injury (5, 7, or 9 years) is the top tier, followed by burning an inhabited structure or property (3, 5, or 8 years), a structure or forest land (2, 4, or 6 years), and property generally (16 months, 2, or 3 years, the only tier that is also the base felony floor). Burning your own personal property is generally not arson at all, unless done with intent to defraud (such as an insurance claim) or it causes injury to another person.",
