    keyRule: "Requires the defendant to have actually received a prohibition before the entry counted as trespass, through oral or written notice from the owner or an authorized agent, a sign posted where reasonably visible, or a court order such as a protective or restraining order with proper service. This makes Virginia's base trespass narrower on its face than states that criminalize any unauthorized entry outright; here, the notice-then-defiance sequence is itself an element. The statute is a single flat misdemeanor tier with no armed or occupied-structure enhancement built into this section.",
