    keyRule: "Covers willfully writing or passing a check with intent to defraud, knowing there are insufficient funds to cover it. Following Proposition 47, a check for $950 or less is punishable only by up to 1 year in county jail, a wobbler ceiling only removed for a defendant with three or more prior forgery or bad-check convictions; a check over $950 can still reach state prison under the general felony sentencing scheme. A protested check for insufficient funds itself creates presumptive evidence of the defendant's knowledge.",
    penaltyClass: "Up to 1 year in county jail (check $950 or less, standard case); felony-eligible under general sentencing (over $950, or 3+ qualifying priors)",
    source: "California Legislature (leginfo), official statute text",
    sourceUrl: "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=PEN&sectionNum=476a.",
