    keyRule: "Applies specifically to a third qualifying act of violence (an enumerated list including murder, voluntary manslaughter, kidnapping, aggravated assault, robbery, carjacking, felony sexual assault, and specified arson offenses, or their equivalents from other jurisdictions), where the defendant has two prior separate convictions for such acts and was at liberty between each. A mandatory term of life imprisonment with no portion suspended, and no parole or earned-credit eligibility, though a narrow conditional-release path exists for defendants 65+ with 5 years served, or 60+ with 10 years served. The Commonwealth must give written notice of its intent to seek this enhancement at least 30 days before trial.",
