    keyRule: "Illinois runs two separate mechanisms. 'Habitual criminal' status applies to a third Class X felony, criminal sexual assault, aggravated kidnapping, or first degree murder conviction where the defendant had two prior separate, sequential convictions for such offenses (first offense committed after July 3, 1980, third offense within 20 years of the first conviction, defendant 21+ at the time of the first offense), triggering MANDATORY natural life imprisonment. A separate, less severe path applies to a defendant 21 or older convicted of a Class 1 or 2 forcible felony with two prior separately-charged forcible felony convictions, elevating sentencing to the Class X range rather than mandatory life. Prior convictions cannot be disclosed to the jury unless the defendant raises the issue, and the defendant has a right to contest them at a post-conviction hearing.",
