    keyRule: "Indiana has NOT decriminalized marijuana at the state level, unlike several other states surveyed in this project; the statute establishes no possession-amount threshold below which conduct is legal. Knowingly possessing marijuana, hash oil, hashish, or salvia, growing/cultivating it, or knowingly failing to destroy plants growing on one's own premises is a Class B misdemeanor at the base tier. It escalates to a Class A misdemeanor with either a prior drug conviction or if the product is packaged as hemp extract but the person knew or reasonably should have known it was actually marijuana or a related substance, and further escalates to a Level 6 felony only when BOTH a prior drug conviction AND a quantity threshold (30+ grams of marijuana, or 5+ grams of hash oil/hashish/salvia) are present together.",
