    keyRule: "Knowingly testifying falsely to a material fact under a legally administered oath or affirmation in an official proceeding, with intent to deceive. Materiality turns on whether the statement could substantially affect (or did substantially affect) the proceeding's course or outcome, regardless of whether it would be independently admissible. A distinctive four-tier grading structure scales with the underlying proceeding's stakes: Class E felony (non-felony proceedings), Class D felony (felony proceedings), Class B felony (a criminal trial to secure a conviction for any felony other than murder), and Class A felony (a criminal trial to secure a murder conviction), the most granular perjury grading structure found among the states surveyed in this project so far. A same-proceeding retraction before the falsity was exposed is an available defense, with the burden on the defendant to raise it.",
