    keyRule: "Rape covers sexual intercourse with another person without consent, with any degree of penetration sufficient and marital status irrelevant. It is a first degree felony, 5 years to life at the standard tier, escalating to a mandatory (non-suspendable) 15-years-to-life if the offense caused serious bodily injury or the defendant was under 18 with a prior serious-sexual-offense conviction, and to a mandatory life sentence without parole if the defendant had a prior conviction for a 'grievous sexual offense' at the time of the rape. Courts retain limited discretion to impose a reduced 10-to-life or 6-to-life term specifically within the 15-to-life tier when justice would be better served, but not within the mandatory-life-without-parole tier.",
